*Unitary Features Embedded in the Constitution:*
- *Residuary Powers (Article 248):* Vested entirely in the Union Parliament (unlike the US Constitution where residuary powers belong to the states).
- *Emergency Powers (Articles 352, 356, 360):* Under Article 356 (President's Rule), the Center can dissolve state governments on the governor's report.
- *Integrated Judiciary & All-India Services:* Single unified supreme court and high courts, along with the IAS and IPS (Article 312).

